        "<strong>Bereshit (<em>בְּרֵאשִׁית</em>) — ‘In the beginning’.</strong> The Hebrew opening word, from which the book takes its Jewish name. Grammatically ambiguous: traditional reading takes it as an absolute (‘In the beginning, God created…’), but Rashi and several modern scholars read it as construct (‘When God began to create…’). The reading affects whether Genesis describes creation <em>ex nihilo</em> or God shaping a pre-existing chaos.",
