        "Polemic against pre-existent matter",
        "<strong>Genesis 1 against Mesopotamian cosmogony.</strong> Where the Babylonian Enuma Elish opens with primordial waters (Apsu and Tiamat) co-eternal with the gods and depicts creation as the violent dismemberment of Tiamat by Marduk, Genesis 1 begins with God already there and matter derivative. The Hebrew verb <em>bara</em> (always with God as subject) and the orderly speech-acts reframe creation as sovereign authorship rather than cosmic conflict. This is theological polemic, not borrowed mythology — Israel knew the surrounding cosmogonies and rejected their ontology of divine struggle.",
