        "<strong>Dictionary (Easton's).</strong> <strong>YEAR H</strong> ebrews shanah, meaning “repetition” or “revolution” (Genesis 1:14; 5:3). Among the ancient Egyptians the year consisted of twelve months of thirty days each, with five days added to make it a complete revolution of the earth round the sun. The Jews reckoned the year in two ways, (1) according to a sacred calendar, in which the year began about the time of the vernal equinox, with the month Abib; and (2) according to a civil calendar, in which the year began about the time of… <em>[Reviewer: condense Easton's entry as needed.]</em>",
