        "Note",
        "Note",
        "<strong>The plural ‘us’ in 1:26.</strong> Scholarly readings include: (1) <em>plural of majesty</em>, like ‘Elohim’; (2) the divine council, where God addresses the angels; (3) a self-deliberation. Christian tradition has often read this as proto-Trinitarian, but most modern Hebrew Bible scholars consider that anachronistic for the original context.",
