        "Easton.",
        "<strong>Dictionary (Easton's).</strong> <strong>SEVEN T</strong> his number occurs frequently in Scripture, and in such connections as lead to the supposition that it has some typical meaning. On the seventh day God rested, and hallowed it (Genesis 2:2, 3). The division of time into weeks of seven days each accounts for many instances of the occurrence of this number. This number has been called the symbol of perfection, and also the symbol of rest. “Jacob’s seven years’ service to Laban; Pharaoh’s seven fat oxen and seven lean ones; the… <em>[Reviewer: condense Easton's entry as needed.]</em>",
