        "Easton.",
        "<strong>Dictionary (Easton's).</strong> <strong>HIDDEKEL</strong> called by the Accadians id Idikla; i.e., “the river of Idikla”, the third of the four rivers of Paradise (Genesis 2:14). Gesenius interprets the word as meaning “the rapid Tigris.” The Tigris rises in the mountains of Armenia, 15 miles south of the source of the Euphrates, which, after pursuing a south-east course, it joins at Kurnah, about 50 miles above Bassorah. Its whole length is about 1,150 miles. <em>[Reviewer: condense Easton's entry as needed.]</em>",
