        "a man will leave his father and his mother",
        "parallel",
        "Parallel",
        "Parallel: Matt 19:5 / Mark 10:7–8 / Eph 5:31 / 1 Cor 6:16",
        '<strong>Genesis 2:24 cited four times in the New Testament.</strong> <a href="index_split_051.html#ch-b60-c19">Matthew 19:5</a> and <a href="index_split_052.html#ch-b61-c10">Mark 10:7–8</a> — Jesus quotes this verse to ground marriage permanence ("what God has joined together, let no one separate"); <a href="index_split_058.html#ch-b69-c5">Ephesians 5:31</a> — Paul cites it to ground the Christ-Church mystery; <a href="index_split_057.html#ch-b66-c6">1 Corinthians 6:16</a> — Paul cites it to argue against sexual immorality. No Old Testament verse is quoted by the New Testament more frequently in connection with marriage. The Ethiopian Tewahedo tradition has historically grounded its theology of marriage in this fourfold citation.',
        "User original",
