        "the serpent",
        "parallel",
        "Parallel",
        "Parallel: Rev 12:9 / Rev 20:2 / John 8:44",
        '<strong>The serpent identified.</strong> Genesis 3 never names the serpent as anything beyond a created beast. The identification with Satan is later canonical synthesis: <a href="index_split_060.html#ch-b86-c12">Revelation 12:9</a> ("the great dragon… the ancient serpent, who is called the devil and Satan"); <a href="index_split_060.html#ch-b86-c20">Revelation 20:2</a> repeats this identification; <a href="index_split_054.html#ch-b63-c8">John 8:44</a> calls the devil "a murderer from the beginning… the father of lies." The Wisdom of Solomon <a href="index_split_036.html#ch-b33-c2">2:24</a> ("through the devil\'s envy death entered the world") is among the earliest texts making the connection explicit.',
