        "Where are you?",
        "comm-modern-critical",
        "Note",
        "Note",
        "<strong>Divine interrogation.</strong> Three questions structure God’s interrogation of the fallen pair: “Where are you?” (3:9), “Who told you that you were naked?” (3:11), “What have you done?” (3:13). Most commentators (Brueggemann, Westermann) read these as pedagogical rather than informational — God knows where Adam is. The pattern of divine questioning persists into Cain (4:9 “Where is your brother?”) and Job 38–41 (the storm questions). Each reveals the questioner’s accountability rather than the questioner’s ignorance — interrogation as a mode of disclosure.",
        "User paraphrase; summarises Brueggemann, Westermann",
