        16,
        "",
        "You will bear children in pain",
        "comm",
        "Note",
        "The triple judgment of Eve, Adam, the serpent",
        "<strong>The structure of the curses.</strong> Genesis 3:14–19 contains three judgments in chiastic order: serpent (3:14–15), woman (3:16), man (3:17–19). Each curse strikes at the central calling: the serpent at its means of motion, the woman at her uniquely reproductive role, the man at his work with the ground. Each also contains a glimmer of continued blessing: the woman will still bear children; the man will still eat bread. The fall does not erase the original blessing of Genesis 1:28 — it complicates it.",
        "User original",
