        "the ground is cursed for your sake",
        "parallel",
        "Parallel",
        "Parallel: Rom 8:20–22 — creation in bondage",
        '<strong>Creation\'s subjection to futility.</strong> Paul reads this curse as the foundation of his cosmic theology: <a href="index_split_056.html#ch-b65-c8">Romans 8:20–22</a> — "the creation was subjected to futility, not willingly, but because of him who subjected it… the whole creation has been groaning together in the pains of childbirth until now." The curse on the ground in Genesis 3 is, for Paul, not local but cosmic — and the redemption in view is not just human but creational. This becomes foundational for the new-creation theme of the New Testament.',
        "User original",
