        "p",
        "Abel and his offering",
        "parallel",
        "Parallel",
        "Parallel: Heb 11:4 — Abel’s faith",
        '<strong>Abel as exemplar of faith.</strong> <a href="index_split_059.html#ch-b78-c11">Hebrews 11:4</a> — "By faith Abel offered to God a more acceptable sacrifice than Cain, through which he was commended as righteous, God commending him by accepting his gifts. And through his faith, though he died, he still speaks." This is the New Testament\'s theological reading of the difference between the offerings: not the substance (animal vs. plant) but the faith of the offerer. Hebrews positions Abel as the first member of the cloud of witnesses, the first martyr.',
