        "<strong>Dictionary (Easton's).</strong> <strong>MUSIC J</strong> ubal was the inventor of musical instruments (Genesis 4:21). The Hebrews were much given to the cultivation of music. Their whole history and literature afford abundant evidence of this. After the Deluge, the first mention of music is in the account of Laban’s interview with Jacob (Genesis 31:27). After their triumphal passage of the Red Sea, Moses and the children of Israel sang their song of deliverance (Exodus 15). But the period of Samuel, David, and Solomon was the… <em>[Reviewer: condense Easton's entry as needed.]</em>",
