        "",
        "",
        "comm",
        "Note",
        "Note",
        "<strong>Genesis 5 lifespans — the Septuagint problem.</strong> The Masoretic Hebrew text and the Septuagint (Greek) give different ages for the patriarchs in this chapter. The Septuagint generally adds 100 years to each patriarch’s age at fatherhood, pushing the Flood’s date significantly earlier. Your Ethiopian-canonical edition follows the Septuagint reckoning, which is why the Flood falls in AM 2243 in this chronology rather than the AM 1656 of the Masoretic text.",
        "User paraphrase; references Septuagint",
