        "word",
        "Note",
        "Note",
        "<strong>Methushelah (<em>מְתוּשֶׁלַח</em>).</strong> A favored etymology breaks the name as <em>met</em> + <em>shelaḥ</em>: “his death → sending,” widely interpreted as “when he dies it (the Flood) is sent.” The arithmetic supports it: in the Masoretic text Methuselah dies in the year of the Flood. (In the LXX/Ethiopian chronology followed by this Bible, the alignment shifts.) The longest-lived patriarch in Scripture; in 1 Enoch 81-82 he becomes the recipient of Enoch’s testamentary teaching.",
