        "Note",
        "<strong>Noḥa (<em>נֹחַ</em>) — word-play on naḥam and nuḥ.</strong> Lamech’s explanation “this one will comfort us” (<em>yenaḥamenū</em>) plays on <em>naḥam</em> (“to comfort”), but the name itself derives from <em>nūḥ</em> (“to rest”). The LXX preserves the wordplay imperfectly with <em>dianapauō</em> (“give rest”). In rabbinic readings (Genesis Rabbah 25:2), Noah’s name signals relief from the curse on the ground in 3:17 — he is born for an agrarian Sabbath.",
