        "1 Enoch (Ethiopian tradition) (-200).",
        '<aside class="note-comm-ethiopian"><strong>1 Enoch (Ethiopian tradition)</strong> <em>Book of the Watchers (1 Enoch 6-11)</em> <small>(c. 200 BC)</small><p>The Nephilim (&#x27;giants&#x27;) of Genesis 6:4 are, in 1 Enoch&#x27;s reading received by Tewahedo, the half-angelic offspring of the Watchers&#x27; union with human women. They are not figures of valor but of disorder; their consumption of all that humans could produce and their turning on humanity is the proximate cause of the Flood. Jude 1:14-15&#x27;s direct quotation of 1 Enoch confirms the New Testament&#x27;s acquaintance with this tradition.</p></aside>',
