        "forty days and forty nights",
        "comm",
        "Note",
        "Note",
        "<strong>Forty days.</strong> The first occurrence of the forty-day motif that structures multiple biblical narratives: Moses on Sinai (Ex 24:18; 34:28), Israel’s spies in Canaan (Num 13:25), Elijah’s wilderness journey to Horeb (1 Kings 19:8), Jonah’s ultimatum to Nineveh (Jonah 3:4), Jesus’s wilderness temptation (Matt 4:2). Forty consistently marks a period of testing, judgment, or transformation. The number combines four (cosmic completeness, four directions) with ten (human totality, fingers/Decalogue) to symbolize a complete bounded period.",
        "User original",
