        "comm-patristic",
        "Note",
        "Note",
        "<strong>God sealed the ark.</strong> The detail is theologically loaded: Noah did not seal himself in; God sealed the ark from outside. The image of divine sealing as protection recurs in Revelation 7:3 (sealing the 144,000 against eschatological judgment) and in Ezekiel 9:4 (the mark on those who grieve). Patristic exegesis (Origen, <em>Homilies on Genesis</em> 2; Hippolytus) reads the ark as type of the church and the divine sealing as type of baptismal initiation, enclosing the faithful through the waters of judgment.",
