        "Only Noah was left",
        "comm",
        "Note",
        "Note",
        "<strong>Remnant theology.</strong> The first occurrence in Scripture of the “remnant” (<em>sheʾar</em>) pattern — when divine judgment falls, a remaining few are preserved. The motif structures prophetic theology (Isa 10:21; Jer 23:3; Ezek 6:8) and reaches its climax in Paul’s Romans 9–11 (the remnant of Israel preserved by grace). Noah’s family is the ur-remnant: not the worthy alone but those graciously preserved through judgment. The pattern challenges any straightforward identification of the saved with the morally superior.",
