        "God remembered Noah",
        "word",
        "Hebrew",
        "Hebrew",
        '<strong>Va-yizkor (<em>וַיִּזְכֹּר</em>).</strong> "And God remembered." The same verb that recurs at decisive moments: God remembers Abraham (Gen 19:29), Rachel (30:22), Israel in Egypt (Exod 2:24), Hannah (1 Sam 1:19). Divine "remembering" in the Hebrew Bible is never about calling something previously forgotten to mind — it is about acting on a prior commitment. The verse marks the structural turning-point of the flood narrative.',
