        "the waters were dried up from the earth",
        "comm-modern-critical",
        "Note",
        "Note",
        "<strong>New creation parallel.</strong> The drying-up parallels Genesis 1: just as the dry land emerged from the primordial waters in 1:9–10, so post-flood land emerges from the receding waters. Many commentators (Wenham, Sailhamer, Mathews) read Genesis 6–9 as a re-creation narrative — the flood is decreation, the receding is re-creation. Noah and his family emerge into a renewed cosmos. 2 Peter 3:6–7 explicitly connects this pattern to eschatology: as the former world was destroyed by water, the present is reserved for fire.",
        "User paraphrase; summarises Wenham, Sailhamer",
