        "Note",
        "<strong>Qeshet (<em>קֶשֶׁת</em>) — ‘bow,’ both rainbow and weapon.</strong> The same Hebrew word means archer’s bow. Some commentators read God’s ‘setting his bow in the cloud’ as God hanging up his weapon — a divine disarmament after the Flood’s violence. The bow points away from earth, toward the heavens.",
