        "<strong>Dictionary (Easton's).</strong> <strong>HUSBANDMAN</strong> one whose business it is to cultivate the ground. It was one of the first occupations, and was esteemed most honourable (Genesis 9:20; 26:12, 14; 37:7, etc.). All the Hebrews, except those engaged in religious services, were husbandmen. (See AGRICULTURE.) <em>[Reviewer: condense Easton's entry as needed.]</em>",
