        "comm-rabbinic",
        "Note",
        "Note",
        "<strong>Japheth in the tents of Shem.</strong> The Hebrew is a wordplay: <em>yapt elohim le-yephet</em>, “may God expand Japheth.” Patristic tradition (Justin, Irenaeus) read this as the Gentile incorporation into Israel’s covenant blessings — Japheth (Indo-European peoples) entering Shem’s (Israel’s) tent through the Church. Targum Pseudo-Jonathan reads the same “dwelling in tents” as a future Roman occupation of Israel. The verse has carried opposite political readings depending on who is hearing it.",
        "User paraphrase; references Irenaeus, Targum, Pseudo-Jonathan",
