        "Note",
        "<strong>The Table of Nations.</strong> Genesis 10 organizes 70 nations descended from Noah’s three sons: Shem (Semites/Asians), Ham (Africans/Egyptians), Japheth (Indo-Europeans/Aegean peoples). The number 70 is significant in Jewish tradition as the number of nations of the world. The genealogy is geographic and ethnic rather than strictly biological — a map of the known world from an Israelite perspective.",
