        "Dictionary",
        "Easton.",
        "<strong>Dictionary (Easton's).</strong> <strong>CANAAN</strong> (1.) The fourth son of Ham (Genesis 10:6). His descendants were under a curse in consequence of the transgression of his father (9:22-27). His eldest son, Zidon, was the father of the Sidonians and Phoenicians. He had eleven sons, who were the founders of as many tribes (10:15-18). (2.) The country which derived its name from the preceding. The name as first used by the Phoenicians denoted only the maritime plain on which Sidon was built. But in the time of Moses and Joshua… <em>[Reviewer: condense Easton's entry as needed.]</em>",
        "Easton's Illustrated Bible Dictionary, M. G. Easton (1897). Public domain.",
