        "Note",
        "Note",
        "<strong>Nimrod — the first ‘mighty one’ on earth.</strong> The Hebrew <em>gibbor</em> (mighty one) is the same word used for the Nephilim in 6:4. The narrator’s ambivalence about Nimrod is debated: some read him as positive (a heroic founder), others as negative (a tyrannical conqueror, founder of Babel and Nineveh). Later Jewish tradition (Josephus, the Babylonian Talmud) consistently casts him negatively as the architect of Babel.",
        "User paraphrase; references Josephus, Talmud",
