        "Canaan became the father of Sidon",
        "comm",
        "Note",
        "The pre-Israelite peoples of the land",
        "<strong>The pre-Israelite Canaanite peoples.</strong> The list of Canaan’s descendants in 10:15–18 is essentially a roster of the peoples Israel will encounter (and largely displace) in the conquest narrative — Sidonians, Hittites, Jebusites, Amorites, Girgashites, Hivites, Arvadites, etc. The same peoples appear in the standard “seven nations” list (Deut 7:1; Josh 3:10) that Israel is commanded to dispossess. Genesis 10 thus encodes the political geography of the promised land before the patriarchs even arrive — when Abraham reaches Canaan in 12:6, every name in the territorial register is already an established political actor.",
        "User original",
