        "Note",
        "<strong>Safah achat (<em>שָׂפָה</em> <em>אַחַת</em>) — ‘one lip.’</strong> The Hebrew idiom is ‘one lip and one set of words.’ The phrasing implies not just shared vocabulary but shared thought, shared understanding. This makes the dispersion at Babel a fragmentation not just of language but of human cognitive unity.",
