        "a tower whose top reaches to the sky",
        "comm-contextual",
        "Note",
        "Note",
        "<strong>Babel and the ziggurat.</strong> The tower described matches the Mesopotamian ziggurat — a stepped temple-pyramid with a shrine at the top. The sin is not architectural ambition per se but the motive: ‘let us make a name for ourselves, lest we be scattered.’ The text reads it as a refusal of the divine commission in Genesis 9:1, ‘fill the earth.’",
