        "Note",
        "Note",
        "<strong>Babel / balal word-play.</strong> The Hebrew text plays on two words: <em>Babel</em> (Babylon, the Akkadian <em>Bab-ilu</em>, ‘gate of the god’) and <em>balal</em> (to confuse). The biblical narrator turns the proud Akkadian etymology (‘gate of god’) into a Hebrew pun on confusion. This is satirical theology — what Babylon called itself, Israel called something else entirely.",
