        "<strong>Dictionary (Easton's).</strong> <strong>ASS</strong> frequently mentioned throughout Scripture. Of the domesticated species we read of, (1.) The she ass (Hebrews ‘athon), so named from its slowness (Genesis 12:16; 45:23; Numbers 22:23; 1 Samuel 9:3). (2.) The male ass (Hebrews hamor), the common working ass of Western Asia, so called from its red colour. Issachar is compared to a strong ass (Genesis 49:14). It was forbidden to yoke together an ass and an ox in the plough (Deuteronomy 22:10). (3.) The ass’s colt (Hebrews ‘air),… <em>[Reviewer: condense Easton's entry as needed.]</em>",
