        13,
        15,
        "",
        "will give all the land which you see",
        "comm",
        "Note",
        "Note",
        "<strong>The unconditional land promise.</strong> The land grant to Abraham’s offspring is “forever” (<em>ʿolam</em>) — a perpetual covenant. This becomes the central theological claim about the land of Israel through millennia of Jewish thought. Christian theology has read it variously: literal-territorial (continued in modern dispensationalism); typological (the land prefigures the heavenly inheritance — Heb 11:16); fulfilled in Christ (Gal 3:16, “the seed” = Christ singular). The verse remains among the most frequently cited in Jewish-Christian-Muslim debates over the land of Israel.",
        "User original",
