        "Easton.",
        "<strong>Dictionary (Easton's).</strong> <strong>OAK T</strong> here are six Hebrew words rendered “oak.” (1.) ‘El occurs only in the word El-paran (Genesis 14:6). The LXX. renders by “terebinth.” In the plural form this word occurs in Isaiah 1:29; 57:5 (A.V. marg. and R.V., “among the oaks”); 61:3 (“trees”). The word properly means strongly, mighty, and hence a strong tree. (2.) ‘Elah, Genesis 35:4, “under the oak which was by Shechem” (R.V. marg., “terebinth”). Isaiah 6:13, A.V., “teil-tree;” R.V., “terebinth.” Isaiah 1:30, R.V. marg.,… <em>[Reviewer: condense Easton's entry as needed.]</em>",
