        "<strong>Dictionary (Easton's).</strong> <strong>ALLIANCE</strong> a treaty between nations, or between individuals, for their mutual advantage. Abraham formed an alliance with some of the Canaanitish princes (Genesis 14:13), also with Abimelech (21:22-32). Joshua and the elders of Israel entered into an alliance with the Gibeonites (Joshua 9:3-27). When the Israelites entered Palestine they were forbidden to enter into alliances with the inhabitants of the country (Leviticus 18:3, 4; 20:22, 23). Solomon formed a league with Hiram (1 Kings… <em>[Reviewer: condense Easton's entry as needed.]</em>",
