        "<strong>Dictionary (Easton's).</strong> <strong>ELIEZER G</strong> od his help. (1.) “Of Damascus,” the “steward” (R.V., “possessor”) of Abraham’s house (Genesis 15:2, 3). It was probably he who headed the embassy sent by Abraham to the old home of his family in Padan-aram to seek a wife for his son Isaac. The account of this embassy is given at length in Genesis 24. (2.) The son of Becher, and grandson of Benjamin (1 Chronicles 7:8). (3.) One of the two sons of Moses, born during his sojourn in Midian (Exodus 18:4; 1 Chronicles 23:15, 17).… <em>[Reviewer: condense Easton's entry as needed.]</em>",
