        "",
        "credited it to him for righteousness",
        "comm",
        "Note",
        "Note",
        "<strong>Imputed righteousness.</strong> One of the most-cited verses in the New Testament. Paul builds his argument in Rom 4 and Gal 3 on this verse, arguing that Abraham was righteous by faith <em>before</em> circumcision (Gen 17) and centuries before Sinai. James 2:23 quotes the same verse to opposite effect — Abraham’s faith was completed in the works of the binding of Isaac (ch 22). Both readings live within the Jewish interpretive horizon of the verse.",
        "User original",
