        "Easton.",
        "<strong>Dictionary (Easton's).</strong> <strong>ISHMAEL G</strong> od hears. (1.) Abraham’s eldest son, by Hagar the concubine (Genesis 16:15; 17:23). He was born at Mamre, when Abraham was eighty-six years of age, eleven years after his arrival in Canaan (16:3; 21:5). At the age of thirteen he was circumcised (17:25). He grew up a true child of the desert, wild and wayward. On the occasion of the weaning of Isaac his rude and wayward spirit broke out in expressions of insult and mockery (21:9, 10); and Sarah, discovering this, said to… <em>[Reviewer: condense Easton's entry as needed.]</em>",
