        "Tewahedo — Ephrem the Syrian",
        "Ephrem the Syrian (360).",
        '<aside class="note-comm-ethiopian"><strong>Ephrem the Syrian</strong> <em>Commentary on Genesis</em> <small>(c. 360 AD)</small><p>&#x27;Is any thing too hard for the Lord?&#x27; Ephrem reads the rhetorical question as the FOUNDATIONAL apologetic for divine omnipotence — and specifically for miracle-faith against rational doubt. The Tewahedo annunciation reading explicitly draws on Gen 18:14 (Sarah&#x27;s incredulity → Isaac&#x27;s miraculous birth) as the OT type of Lk 1:37 (&#x27;for with God nothing shall be impossible&#x27; — the angel to Mary). Ephrem&#x27;s exegesis pins the typological chain.</p></aside>',
        "Ephrem the Syrian, Commentary on Genesis, Section XVIII.14. NPNF Series 2, vol. 13, ed. J. Gwynn / Schaff (1898). PD.",
