        "I have sworn by myself",
        "comm",
        "Note",
        "Note",
        "<strong>Oath by self.</strong> Yahweh swears by himself — the only being greater than whom there is none. Hebrews 6:13–18 develops this verse extensively: God’s oath-by-self provides “two unchangeable things” (promise + oath) by which it is impossible for God to lie. The covenant’s certainty rests not on any external guarantor but on God’s own being. The verse is cited in Jewish liturgy (the daily morning blessings) and underlies the theological claim that covenant promise is unconditional from God’s side.",
        "User original",
