        "Dictionary",
        "Easton.",
        "<strong>Dictionary (Easton's).</strong> <strong>KEDAR</strong> dark-skinned, the second son of Ishmael (Genesis 25:13). It is the name for the nomadic tribes of Arabs, the Bedouins generally (Isaiah 21:16; 42:11; 60:7; Jeremiah 2:10; Ezekiel 27:21), who dwelt in the north-west of Arabia. They lived in black hair-tents (Cant. 1:5). To “dwell in the tents of Kedar” was to be cut off from the worship of the true God (Psalm 120:5). The Kedarites suffered at the hands of Nebuchadnezzar (Jeremiah 49:28, 29). <em>[Reviewer: condense Easton's entry as needed.]</em>",
