        "angels of God were ascending and descending",
        "comm",
        "Note",
        "Note",
        '<strong>Jacob’s ladder.</strong> The Hebrew <em>sullam</em> may better translate as "ramp" or "stairway" — likely the same architectural image as the ziggurat of Genesis 11, but here legitimately connecting heaven and earth. Jesus alludes to this verse in John 1:51 ("you will see heaven open, and the angels of God ascending and descending on the Son of Man") — placing himself in the role of the ladder.',
        "User original",
