        "<strong>Dictionary (Easton's).</strong> <strong>STONE S</strong> tones were commonly used for buildings, also as memorials of important events (Genesis 28:18; Joshua 24:26, 27; 1 Samuel 7:12, etc.). They were gathered out of cultivated fields (Isaiah 5:2; comp. 2 Kings 3:19). This word is also used figuratively of believers (1 Peter 2:4, 5), and of the Messiah (Psalm 118:22; Isaiah 28:16; Matthew 21:42; Acts 4:11, etc.). In Daniel 2:45 it refers also to the Messiah. He is there described as “cut out of the mountain.” (See ROCK.) A “heart… <em>[Reviewer: condense Easton's entry as needed.]</em>",
