        "God has judged me",
        "comm",
        "Note",
        "Note",
        "<strong>Dan = he judged.</strong> Rachel names the first surrogate-son Dan (<em>Dan</em>, <em>דָּן</em>, from the verb <em>din</em>, “to judge”). She means Dan’s birth is divine judicial vindication of her plea. The verb <em>din</em> appears most commonly in legal contexts; Rachel’s appeal frames her relation to God as forensic — she has been heard in cosmic court. The Tribe of Dan later becomes the legendary tribe of judges (Samson, Judges 13–16), and Genesis 49:16 pronounces “Dan shall judge his people.” The pun encoded in his name’s etymology persists into Israel’s tribal identity.",
        "User original",
