        "<strong>Dictionary (Easton's).</strong> <strong>DOWRY</strong> (mohar; i.e., price paid for a wife, Genesis 34:12; Exodus 22:17; 1 Samuel 18:25), a nuptial present; some gift, as a sum of money, which the bridegroom offers to the father of his bride as a satisfaction before he can receive her. Jacob had no dowry to give for his wife, but he gave his services (Genesis 29:18; 30:20; 34:12). <em>[Reviewer: condense Easton's entry as needed.]</em>",
