        "she named him Benoni, but his father named him Benjamin",
        "comm",
        "Note",
        "Note",
        '<strong>Ben-oni / Benjamin.</strong> Rachel names her dying-birth child <em>Ben-oni</em> ("son of my sorrow"); Jacob renames him <em>Binyamin</em> ("son of the right hand," or "son of the south"). One of the few moments in scripture where a parental naming is overridden. Jacob’s renaming is theological — he refuses to let a beloved son carry his mother’s death as his lifelong identity. Rachel is buried on the road to Bethlehem (35:19) — her tomb becomes a pilgrimage site referenced in Jer 31:15 and Matt 2:18.',
        "User original",
