        "comm-ethiopian",
        "Tewahedo — Ephrem the Syrian",
        "Ephrem the Syrian (360).",
        '<aside class="note-comm-ethiopian"><strong>Ephrem the Syrian</strong> <em>Commentary on Genesis</em> <small>(c. 360 AD)</small><p>&#x27;And he dreamed yet another dream, and told it his brethren, and said, Behold, I have dreamed a dream more; and, behold, the sun and the moon and the eleven stars made obeisance to me&#x27;. Ephrem reads Joseph&#x27;s astral dream as a Marian prefiguration: Rev 12:1 (&#x27;a woman clothed with the sun, and the moon under her feet, and upon her head a crown of twelve stars&#x27;) reuses Joseph&#x27;s imagery for Mary. Tewahedo Marian iconography preserves the Rev-12 crown imagery, reading Joseph&#x27;s dream as the OT root.</p></aside>',
        "Ephrem the Syrian, Commentary on Genesis, Section XXXVII.9. NPNF Series 2, vol. 13, ed. J. Gwynn / Schaff (1898). PD.",
