    (
        38,
        18,
        "",
        "Your signet and your cord, and your staff",
        "comm",
        "Note",
        "Note",
        "<strong>Identifying tokens.</strong> Tamar requires three identifying tokens — signet (<em>chotam</em>), cord (<em>patil</em>), staff (<em>matteh</em>) — the most specific identification possible. The signet was a personal seal-stamp (typically worn on cord around neck), used for legal authentication. Each item identifies Judah uniquely. The triple-pledge ensures Tamar can prove her claim against any denial — anticipating exactly the courtroom moment at 38:25–26. The detail also reveals Judah as economically secure (signet-owning) but morally careless (handing over his identity for a sexual transaction).",
        "User original",
    ),
