        "<strong>Dictionary (Easton's).</strong> <strong>CUP</strong> a wine-cup (Genesis 40:11, 21), various forms of which are found on Assyrian and Egyptian monuments. All Solomon’s drinking vessels were of gold (1 Kings 10: 21). The cups mentioned in the New Testament were made after Roman and Greek models, and were sometimes of gold (Revelation 17:4). The art of divining by means of a cup was practiced in Egypt (Genesis 44:2-17), and in the East generally. The “cup of salvation” (Psalm 116:13) is the cup of thanksgiving for the great… <em>[Reviewer: condense Easton's entry as needed.]</em>",
