        "Dictionary",
        "Easton.",
        "<strong>Dictionary (Easton's).</strong> <strong>MEADOW</strong> (1.) Hebrews ha’ahu (Genesis 41:2, 18), probably an Egyptain word transferred to the Hebrew; some kind of reed or water-plant. In the Revised Version it is rendered “reed-grass”, i.e., the sedge or rank grass by the river side. (2.) Hebrews ma’areh (Judges 20:33), pl., “meadows of Gibeah” (R.V., after the LXX., “Maareh-geba”). Some have adopted the rendering “after Gibeah had been left open.” The Vulgate translates the word “from the west.” <em>[Reviewer: condense Easton's entry as needed.]</em>",
