        "Easton.",
        "<strong>Dictionary (Easton's).</strong> <strong>CHAIN</strong> (1.) A part of the insignia of office. A chain of gold was placed about Joseph’s neck (Genesis 41:42); and one was promised to Daniel (5:7). It is used as a symbol of sovereignty (Ezekiel 16:11). The breast-plate of the high-priest was fastened to the ephod by golden chains (Exodus 39:17, 21). (2.) It was used as an ornament (Proverbs 1:9; Cant. 1:10). The Midianites adorned the necks of their camels with chains (Judges 8:21, 26). (3.) Chains were also used as fetters… <em>[Reviewer: condense Easton's entry as needed.]</em>",
