        "<strong>Dictionary (Easton's).</strong> <strong>ON</strong> light; the sun, (Genesis 41:45, 50), the great seat of sun-worship, called also Bethshemesh (Jeremiah 43:13) and Aven (Ezekiel 30:17), stood on the east bank of the Nile, a few miles north of Memphis, and near Cairo, in the north-east. The Vulgate and the LXX. Versions have “Heliopolis” (“city of the sun”) instead of On in Genesis and of Aven in Ezekiel. The “city of destruction” Isaiah speaks of (19:18, marg. “of Heres;” Hebrews ‘Ir-ha-heres, which some MSS. read… <em>[Reviewer: condense Easton's entry as needed.]</em>",
