        "",
        "by which he indeed divines",
        "comm",
        "Note",
        "Note",
        "<strong>Joseph’s divining cup.</strong> Joseph’s steward attributes divinatory practice to his master’s silver cup — hydromancy (water-divination by observing patterns in cup) was an Egyptian practice. The detail is layered: either Joseph genuinely uses divination (problematic given Mosaic prohibitions later), or the steward exaggerates for dramatic effect, or Joseph plays the role of an Egyptian official. Most commentators favor the third reading — the cup-divination is part of Joseph’s elaborate test-setup. The verse highlights how Joseph speaks within Egyptian categories while operating from covenant theology — bicultural performance, not actual divination.",
        "User original",
