        "Dictionary",
        "Easton.",
        "<strong>Dictionary (Easton's).</strong> <strong>PLOUGH</strong> first referred to in Genesis 45:6, where the Authorized Version has “earing,” but the Revised Version “ploughing;” next in Exodus 34:21 and Deuteronomy 21:4. The plough was originally drawn by oxen, but sometimes also by asses and by men. (See AGRICULTURE.) <em>[Reviewer: condense Easton's entry as needed.]</em>",
