    (
        46,
        8,
        "",
        "These are the names of the children of Israel",
        "comm",
        "Note",
        "Note",
        "<strong>Genealogy framing the descent.</strong> The full genealogical list (46:8–27) frames the descent into Egypt with the named tribal patriarchs — preserving family identity at the moment of geographic transition. The same opening phrase (“These are the names of the children of Israel”) becomes the title of the next book (Exodus 1:1). The literary continuity directly links Genesis 46 to Exodus 1, treating the narrative as a single arc despite the book division. The genealogical inclusio frames Egypt as a chapter in family history, not a destination.",
        "User original",
    ),
