        "<strong>Dictionary (Easton's).</strong> <strong>GERSHON</strong> =Ger’shom expulsion, the eldest of Levi’s three sons (Genesis 46:11; Exodus 6:16). In the wilderness the sons of Gershon had charge of the fabrics of the tabernacle when it was moved from place to place, the curtains, veils, tent-hangings (Numbers 3: 21-26). Thirteen Levitical cities fell to the lot of the Gershonites (Joshua 21:27-33). <em>[Reviewer: condense Easton's entry as needed.]</em>",
