        49,
        7,
        "",
        "I will divide them in Jacob",
        "comm",
        "Note",
        "Note",
        "<strong>Simeon and Levi divided.</strong> The “curse” on Simeon and Levi for the Shechem violence (ch 34) takes the form of dispersion. Simeon’s tribal allotment in Joshua 19:1–9 lies entirely within Judah’s territory — by the time of the conquest, Simeon has been functionally absorbed. Levi’s “dispersion” takes a different form: as the priestly tribe, Levites have no contiguous territory but cities scattered throughout Israel (Numbers 35; Joshua 21). The same curse — “divided in Jacob, scattered in Israel” — is fulfilled in opposite ways: Simeon shrinks; Levi sanctified. The pattern teaches that judgment can transform into vocation.",
        "User original",
